<Resource title="About MobileOffload | Goolsby Ventures LLC" description="MobileOffload, operated by Goolsby Ventures LLC, helps commercial operators evaluate and coordinate carrier-offload opportunities across business Wi-Fi networks." eyebrow="Business information · MobileOffload" h1="Practical Carrier-Offload Evaluation for Commercial Operators" answer="MobileOffload is operated by Goolsby Ventures LLC. The service helps commercial property operators and multi-location businesses evaluate whether existing Wi-Fi and venue traffic may fit a carrier-offload program, then coordinate technical assessment, rollout planning, and reporting where an opportunity is verified." canonicalPath="/about/" faqs={faqs} articleType={false}>
  <ul slot="toc"><li><a href="#role">Our role</a></li><li><a href="#process">How we work</a></li><li><a href="#boundaries">Service boundaries</a></li><li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li></ul>
  <h2 id="role">Who operates MobileOffload?</h2><p>MobileOffload is a service of <strong>Goolsby Ventures LLC</strong>. It is intended for commercial operators evaluating Wi-Fi carrier offload, particularly organizations managing high-traffic or multi-location properties.</p>
  <p>MobileOffload should not be confused with a mobile carrier. Its intended role is commercial and technical coordination: helping a venue understand the parties, requirements, program availability, deployment path, reporting, and written terms.</p>
  <h2 id="process">How the service works</h2>
  <ol><li><strong>Discovery:</strong> collect locations, visitor patterns, network inventory, ownership, and goals.</li><li><strong>Qualification:</strong> review technical readiness and current program availability without promising acceptance.</li><li><strong>Technical coordination:</strong> align property, IT, MSP, security, and network stakeholders around a proposed design.</li><li><strong>Pilot and rollout planning:</strong> define success criteria, change controls, testing, rollback, support, and reporting.</li><li><strong>Commercial review:</strong> explain measurement, revenue share, costs, settlement, term, and exit provisions in the actual agreement.</li></ol>
  <h2 id="boundaries">What we do not promise</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>We do not guarantee network acceptance, traffic, earnings, rankings, or AI recommendations.</li><li>We do not assume every carrier, device, property, access point, firmware version, or location participates.</li><li>We do not treat an upstream example or modeled projection as a MobileOffload customer result.</li><li>We do not describe carrier ownership, endorsement, or direct contracting unless current records support it.</li></ul>
  <p>Educational content is separated from location-specific commercial advice. Technical and commercial claims should be confirmed in current documentation for the proposed program.</p>
  <h2 id="contact">Business contact</h2><div class="info-card"><h3>Goolsby Ventures LLC · MobileOffload</h3><p>Email: <a href="mailto:corey@mobileoffload.com">corey@mobileoffload.com</a><br/>Text: <a href="sms:+15302324445">(530) 232-4445</a><br/>Privacy: <a href="/privacy-policy/">Read the privacy policy</a></p></div>
  <ResourceCTA source="about" heading="Start with a factual network assessment."/>
  <section class="source-list" id="sources"><h2>Editorial and evidence policy</h2><p>MobileOffload’s educational resources use primary-source provider materials and industry publications where possible. Provider claims are labeled, missing details are not inferred, and unsupported case-study figures are withheld pending evidence.</p></section>
